#X obj 695 8 xfade~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 286 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The control float value in the range [0 \, N−1] selects
the crossfade between the input signals: [0 \, 1) fades between the
first and second signal \, [1 \, 2) between the second and third \,
and so on. Integer values produce a single input \, fractional values
produce a blend of two neighbouring inputs.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 209 • Smooth switching between audio sources — crossfading
between several oscillators \, samplers or live inputs without clicks
\, for example selecting an active sound source by a single continuous
parameter.;
#X text 250 279 • Layered transitions in performance — morphing between
different textures \, effects or voices on the fly \, with a musical
rather than abrupt transition \, controlled from a single knob \, LFO
or automation curve.;
#X text 50 412 simple 2-channel crossfade;
